# Module End-to-End Completion Checklist

## Ground Rule

No deferral. No “minimum viable” scope. No fake green. No partial module claims. A module is not considered complete unless its full route, API, service, DB, auth, workflow, seed data, UI, observability, and role behavior work end-to-end in the live workspace.

Each module must be checked and fixed as a complete vertical slice.

---

## Completion Definition for Every Module

A module is **DONE** only when all of the following are true:

| Layer           | Required Proof                                                                     |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Navigation      | Route appears only for allowed roles and opens without blank page or redirect loop |
| Frontend Route  | Component renders with no Angular DI/runtime crash                                 |
| API Contract    | Every API called by the page exists and returns valid JSON shape                   |
| Gateway Routing | Gateway has correct prefix mapping to the owning service                           |
| Service Handler | Backend handler exists, has correct middleware, and returns expected data          |
| DB Schema       | Required public/dos/platform_dauth/tenant-schema tables and columns exist          |
| Seed Data       | Tenant has enough realistic records to make the page useful                        |
| AuthN           | Valid KC/DAuth token is accepted by all involved services                          |
| AuthZ           | Role/permission rules work without platform-admin bypass                           |
| SoD             | Separation-of-duties rules exist or are explicitly proven not applicable           |
| Workflow        | Required tasks/approvals/events exist and execute                                  |
| Events          | Domain events/outbox/notifications work where expected                             |
| Observability   | Logs, metrics, and error paths are visible and correlated                          |
| UI Quality      | No broken cards, dead buttons, missing widgets, or placeholder 404 panels          |
| Negative Test   | Unauthorized role is blocked from write/high-risk actions                          |

