## Fix Rules

1. Fix route/API/DB contract at the source. Do not hide broken endpoints behind fake success.
2. Use real seed data only. No dark/demo junk unrelated to Shahin.
3. No platform-admin shortcut for tenant users.
4. Every role must be tenant-scoped unless explicitly platform-level.
5. Every write action must have an authorization and audit proof.
6. Every workflow action must create or update a real workflow/task/event row.
7. Every module must have at least one negative test.
8. If a UI calls a legacy endpoint, either wire the endpoint correctly or change the UI to the canonical route.
9. If a table column is missing, decide explicitly: migration vs contract change. Avoid permanent NULL shims.
10. Do not mark production-ready until all module gates pass.

